<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 5.315 bln levs 3-mth float T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 5.315 bln levs 3-mth float T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on Wednesday sold 5.315 billion levs of three-month floater coupon T-bills, yielding 60.95 percent to maturity, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no par value or minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the central bank's main interest rate, now set at 18 percent monthly or 216 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Price in percent of par: </p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3022797024</p>
<p> Type			    floater coupon</p>
<p> Term			    three months</p>
<p> Auction date		  March 26</p>
<p> Issue date		    March 26</p>
<p> Maturity date		 June 25</p>
<p> Bids received		 6,015 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   95.47</p>
<p> Bids approved		 5,315 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  95.59 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     60.95 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
